              "step": "Step 4: Determine Net Heat Absorbed $Q$ and Polytropic Heat Capacity $C_m$",
              "detail": "<p>By the First Law of Thermodynamics:</p>\n\n<div class=\"math-display\">$$Q = \\Delta U + W = -4803.3 + 7685.2 = +2881.9\\text{ J}$$</div>\n\n<p>The molar polytropic heat capacity is derived via $C_m = C_{v, m} + \\frac{R}{1 - n}$:</p>\n\n<div class=\"math-display\">$$C_{v, m} = \\frac{R}{\\gamma - 1} = \\frac{8.314}{0.40} = 20.785\\text{ J/(mol}\\cdot\\text{K)}$$</div>\n\n<div class=\"math-display\">$$\\frac{R}{1 - n} = \\frac{8.314}{1 - 1.25} = \\frac{8.314}{-0.25} = -33.256\\text{ J/(mol}\\cdot\\text{K)}$$</div>\n\n<div class=\"math-display\">$$C_m = 20.785 - 33.256 = -12.47\\text{ J/(mol}\\cdot\\text{K)}$$</div>\n\n<p>Notice that the polytropic molar heat capacity is negative: as the gas absorbs heat, its temperature decreases because the work done on the surroundings exceeds the heat supplied.</p>"
