              "step": "Step 2: Integrated Clausius-Clapeyron Equation",
              "detail": "<p>Approximating steam as an ideal gas ($v_{\\text{steam}} \\approx R T / P M$) and neglecting $v_{\\text{liquid}}$:</p>\n\n<div class=\"math-display\">$$\\frac{d \\ln P}{dT} = \\frac{L_{v, m}}{R T^2} \\implies \\ln\\left(\\frac{P}{P_0}\\right) = -\\frac{L_{v, m}}{R} \\left( \\frac{1}{T} - \\frac{1}{T_0} \\right)$$</div>\n\n<p>Molar latent heat: $L_{v, m} = L_v \\times M = (2.257 \\times 10^6)(0.018015\\text{ kg/mol}) = 40660\\text{ J/mol}$.</p>\n\n<div class=\"math-display\">$$\\ln\\left(\\frac{70.0}{101.3}\\right) = \\ln(0.6910) = -0.3696$$</div>\n\n<div class=\"math-display\">$$\\frac{L_{v, m}}{R} = \\frac{40660}{8.314} = 4890.5\\text{ K}$$</div>\n\n<div class=\"math-display\">$$-0.3696 = -4890.5 \\left( \\frac{1}{T} - \\frac{1}{373.15} \\right)$$</div>\n\n<div class=\"math-display\">$$\\frac{1}{T} - 0.0026799 = \\frac{0.3696}{4890.5} = 7.5575 \\times 10^{-5}$$</div>\n\n<div class=\"math-display\">$$\\frac{1}{T} = 0.0026799 + 0.00007558 = 0.0027555\\text{ K}^{-1}$$</div>\n\n<div class=\"math-display\">$$T = \\frac{1}{0.0027555} = 362.91\\text{ K} = 89.76^\\circ\\text{C}$$</div>"
